        {
          "id": "1781705164337",
          "code": "INCIDENT_QUERY_ANALYZER",
          "type": "AGENT",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Incident query Analyzer",
            "type": "PRIVATE",
            "specification": {
              "maxInteractions": 20,
              "agentRole": "You are a  code enforcement Incident Analyzer Agent, responsible for task analysis, decomposition, and intelligent delegation within the code enforcement Incident Management System. You provide summary to Code technician based on incoming Incidents.\n\nPrimary Tasks:\n- Receive queries and break down complex instructions into smaller subtasks.\n- Assign each subtask to the most suitable available tools\n\nIf a task cannot be handled by the available agents:\n- Respond with a clear, user-friendly explanation of supported capabilities based on known agents.",
              "inputs": [],
              "outputSpecification": " ",
              "summarizationMode": "Default",
              "summarizationPrompt": "Based on the information through the chat history and/or tool call responses, construct a clear, professional, and user-friendly answer to address the user's original query. \nconstruct an answer that addresses the user's original query. \nYour answer should be directed towards the user and should be friendly, professional, \nand concise. If you are not able to answer the user's question based on the tool calls or through the chat history, \nyou should let them know that you do not have access to that information. \n \n--ANSWER REQUIREMENTS-- \nYour answer should be based only on the information available to you in the tool calling chat \nhistory. You should never invent or make up answers. If the question requires you to synthesize \nanswers across several tool responses, you should do that. Note that some information may need \nto be summarized from across multiple places in a given object. Use your inference and semantic \nknowledge to derive the answer from the data without inventing anything. \n \n--ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS-- \n* Do not mention tool calls, chat history, underlying operations, or system processes. \n* Keep the response natural and conversational without unnecessary preambles. \n* Provide a direct and engaging response without phrases like \"Based on tool calls\" or similar references. \n* Do not append any characters or trailing Periods (.) at the end of valid URLs. \n* If link is generated by DeepLink tool do not remove from response."
            },
            "toolCodes": [],
            "topicCodes": []
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6490.381393523207,
            "y": 6260.93626640616
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1781705178489_1",
              "name": "message",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$app.$OraMessageHint}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1781705178489_2",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "1. Summarize Incoming Incidents\n-Call Get_incomingIncidents to retrieve ALL daily incidents with \"reported\" status and no technician assigned\n-Identify and summarize any duplicates (e.g., by street/address); list Incident IDs and reasons for the duplicates.\n-Count and report the total number of qualifying incoming incidents.\n-Always include the Review Due Date, marking it \"Overdue\" if past, and indicate days overdue.\n-Always include available code technicians for assignment\n-IMPORTANT : Response should include Table1: list of all incidents, Table2: duplicates grouped, Table3: code technicians\n-TABLE 2 - DUPLICATES\n-Incident IDs : Incident Details Link with all incidents grouped as duplicates\n-Description\n-Address\n- Duplicate - Duplicates  \n\n\n2. High Priority Unassigned Incidents\n-Use tool Get_high_priority_incoming_incident.\n-List all incidents with high priority and no technician assigned\n-Include review due date and flag if overdue.\n-Display the total count.\n\n3. Overdue Unassigned Incidents\n-Call Get_unassigned_overdue_Incidents.\n-Indicate how many days each is overdue.\n-Suggest assigning a technician, providing a list via getall_publicSectorSearchCodeTechnicians.\n\n4. Active Incidents\n-Call get_Active_Incidents_Finder to summarize active incidents.\n\n5. Incident Search by Specific Input\n-Call getall_publicSectorIncidents, passing user input as the search value.\n\n6. List Available Technicians\n-Use getall_publicSectorSearchCodeTechnicians for technician availability.\nAllow users to select a technician for assignments.\n\n7. Code Technician Assignment Requests\nSTEP1 : Use getall_publicSectorSearchCodeTechnicians tool to get all the code technicians\nSTEP2: Store the above code technician response in an object called codeTechnicians as this format {\"CodeTechnicianName\": <DisplayName> , \"CodeTechnicianId\" : <PersonId>} for each technician\nSTEP3: Using the user input name of code technician find the CodeTechnicianId and store it as pPersonId\nSTEP4: get the IncidentKey of the selected incident using tool Code Enforcement Incidents Updates and store it as pIncidentKey\nSTEP5: Update the incident using tool Code Enforcement Incidents Updates, business function update_incident. IMPORTANT : pass the pIncidentKey and pPersonId. \n\n8. Update the priority of Incident\nThe \"Priority\" of the incident can be updated to \n- High priority with payload {\"Priority\" : \"ORA_H\"} set pPriority=\"ORA_H\" or\n-Low priority with payload {\"Priority\":\"ORA_N\"} set  pPriority=\"ORA_N\"\n-Call tool update_incident IMPORTANT : pass the pIncidentKey and pPriority. \n\nShow Incident Id as Deep link.\n\nGentle Reminders:\n-Always verify data, highlight overdues, ensure duplicate detection, and provide professional HTML tables.\n-Never skip required fields or overdue remarks."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "1781706645285",
          "code": "GET_SMART_SUMMARY_FOR_INCOMING_INCIDENTS",
          "type": "CODE",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get Smart Summary for Incoming Incidents",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const reportedIncidents = $context.$nodes.GET_REPORTED_INCIDENTS.$output.items || [];\nconst incidentAiResults = $context.$nodes.GET_AI_RESULTS.$output.items || [];\n\nconsole.log(\"Debuggign source code\");\nconst normalizeAi = (value) => {\n  if (value === null || value === undefined) return null;\n\n  if (typeof value === \"string\") {\n    try {\n      return JSON.parse(value);\n    } catch {\n      return null;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return value;\n};\n\nconst escapeStrings = (obj) => {\n  if (obj === null || obj === undefined) return obj;\n\n  if (typeof obj === \"string\") {\n    return obj.replace(/\\n/g, \"\\\\n\").replace(/\\t/g, \"\\\\t\");\n  }\n\n  if (Array.isArray(obj)) {\n    return obj.map(escapeStrings);\n  }\n\n  if (typeof obj === \"object\") {\n    const out = {};\n    for (const key in obj) {\n      if (key === \"@context\") continue;\n      out[key] = escapeStrings(obj[key]);\n    }\n    return out;\n  }\n\n  return obj;\n};\n\nconst formatDate = (value) => {\n  if (!value) return \"\";\n  const d = new Date(value);\n  if (Number.isNaN(d.getTime())) return String(value);\n  return d.toISOString().split(\"T\")[0];\n};\n\nconst formatAddress = (incident) => {\n  const parts = [\n    incident.PropertyAddress1,\n    incident.PropertyCity,\n    incident.PropertyState,\n    incident.PropertyPostalCode\n  ].filter(Boolean);\n\n  return parts.join(\", \");\n};\n\nconst getPrimaryAction = (aiContent) => {\n  if (!aiContent) return \"ORA_SCHEDULE\";\n\n  if (aiContent.DuplicateCheck?.DuplicateFound === true) {\n    return \"ORA_DUPLICATE\";\n  }\n\n  if (aiContent.Reroute?.RerouteNeeded === true) {\n    return \"ORA_REROUTE\";\n  }\n\n  if (aiContent.PriorityRecommendation?.UpdatePriority === true) {\n    return \"ORA_PRIORITY\";\n  }\n\n  const actions = Array.isArray(aiContent.RecommendedAction)\n    ? aiContent.RecommendedAction\n    : [];\n\n  if (actions.includes(\"ORA_DUPLICATE\")) return \"ORA_DUPLICATE\";\n  if (actions.includes(\"ORA_REROUTE\")) return \"ORA_REROUTE\";\n  if (actions.includes(\"ORA_PRIORITY\")) return \"ORA_PRIORITY\";\n\n  return \"ORA_SCHEDULE\";\n};\n\nconst buildSummary = (incident) => {\n  const desc = incident.IssueDescription || \"\";\n  const reportedDate = formatDate(incident.CreationDate);\n  const address = formatAddress(incident);\n\n  return `Issue: ${desc}. Reported: ${reportedDate}. Address: ${address}.`;\n};\n\nconst aiMap = new Map(\n  incidentAiResults.map(item => [\n    String(item.ResultId),\n    normalizeAi(item.Content)\n  ])\n);\n\nconst data = reportedIncidents.map((incident) => {\n  const aiContentRaw = aiMap.get(String(incident.IncidentKey)) || null;\n  const primaryAction = getPrimaryAction(aiContentRaw);\n\n  const baseItem = {\n    Title: incident.IncidentId || \"\",\n    Summary: buildSummary(incident),\n    badgeText: \"\",\n    Priority: \"medium\"\n  };\n\n  if (primaryAction === \"ORA_DUPLICATE\") {\n    const parentMatch = aiContentRaw?.DuplicateCheck?.matches?.[0] || {};\n    return {\n      ...baseItem,\n      badgeText: \"Close As Duplicate\",\n      AdditionalAction: {\n        label: \"Close\",\n        command: `ora.Invoke(\"CloseAsDuplicate\", { \"actionName\":\"CloseAsDuplicate\", \"IncidentID\":\"${incident.IncidentId || \"\"}\", \"IncidentKey\":\"${incident.IncidentKey || \"\"}\", \"ParentKey\":\"${parentMatch.TransactionKey || \"\"}\", \"ParentId\":\"${parentMatch.TransactionId || \"\"}\"})`\n      }\n    };\n  }\n\n  if (primaryAction === \"ORA_REROUTE\") {\n    return {\n      ...baseItem,\n      badgeText: \"Reroute\",\n      AdditionalAction: {\n        label: \"Reroute\",\n        command: `ora.Invoke(\"Reroute\", {\"actionName\":\"Reroute\", \"IncidentID\":\"${incident.IncidentId || \"\"}\", \"IncidentKey\":\"${incident.IncidentKey || \"\"}\", \"NewIssueSubtype\":\"${aiContentRaw?.Reroute?.ReroutedTo?.IssueSubtype || \"\"}\"})`\n      }\n    };\n  }\n\n  if (primaryAction === \"ORA_PRIORITY\") {\n    return {\n      ...baseItem,\n      badgeText: \"Update Priority\",\n      AdditionalAction: {\n        label: \"Priority\",\n        command: `ora.Invoke(\"UpdatePriority\", {\"actionName\":\"UpdatePriority\", \"IncidentID\":\"${incident.IncidentId || \"\"}\", \"IncidentKey\":\"${incident.IncidentKey || \"\"}\", \"Priority\":\"ORA_H\"})`\n      }\n    };\n  }\n\n  return {\n    ...baseItem,\n    badgeText: \"Schedule Inspection\",\n    AdditionalAction: {\n      label: \"Schedule\",\n      command: `ora.Invoke(\"ScheduleInspection\", {\"actionName\":\"ScheduleInspection\", \"IncidentID\":\"${incident.IncidentId || \"\"}\", \"IncidentKey\":\"${incident.IncidentKey || \"\"}\", \"ReviewDueDate\":\"${incident.ReviewDueDate || \"\"}\"})`\n    }\n  };\n});\n\nreturn {\n  messageListWidget: {\n    Data: data\n  }\n};"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6815.971097664822,
            "y": 5955.181863799188
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1781706681535"
          },
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "id": "1781706681535",
          "code": "FORMAT_PANEL_DATA",
          "type": "CODE",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "format Panel data",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const raw =  $context.$nodes.GET_SMART_SUMMARY_FOR_INCOMING_INCIDENTS.$output.result \n\nif (!raw) {\n  return {\n    messageListWidget: {\n      Data: []\n    }\n  };\n}\n\nif (typeof raw === \"string\") {\n  try {\n    return JSON.parse(raw);\n  } catch {\n    return {\n      messageListWidget: {\n        Data: []\n      }\n    };\n  }\n}\n\nreturn raw;"
          },
